From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:52:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 70/85] hjviewer: the desktop home's menus and the ID
 suggestions

U12: the ID suggestions under the remote ID field (desktop and phone)
are drawn like the app's menus: a card with the thin border, radius 12
and the theme's menu shadow, as wide as the field. Each suggestion is a
small PC row: the cards' 32 px soft tile, the name in 14/600 with the
online dot, user@host in 12 px secondary text and, beside an alias, the
ID spaced by formatID in tabular digits at the row's end; rows hover in
the palette's hover colour. The new panel lives in hjv_autocomplete.dart
(its sizes and texts in hjv_suggestions.dart, plain Dart with a test)
and the connection pages switch to it; AutocompletePeerTile stays.

U22: the title bar's settings button is a gear (settings_outlined), as
it opens the settings and no menu. The ID card's more button opens a
small menu at the pointer: Copy ID, Change ID (to Security, when the
settings and the ID change are not disabled) and Settings; its tooltip
is "More". A right-click on a desktop PC card opens the card's menu at
the pointer, as its more button does; a right-click on that button
still opens its menu only once.
